WEBVTT

1
00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:36.665
Rule 1, we eat separately.

2
00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:40.452
In fact,
wouldn't it be uncomfortable

3
00:01:40.532 --> 00:01:42.299
to sit at a table
with a stranger?

4
00:01:43.465 --> 00:01:46.885
Rule 2, saving electricity!
Save water!

5
00:01:46.965 --> 00:01:49.465
Do you know saving
is the best income?

6
00:01:50.532 --> 00:01:51.788
Rule 3,

7
00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.365
a personal space
must be respected.

8
00:01:57.499 --> 00:02:00.019
Never intrude on the red line.

9
00:02:00.099 --> 00:02:02.785
Yellow is a common area.

10
00:02:02.865 --> 00:02:04.885
Your color is blue.

11
00:02:04.965 --> 00:02:07.332
(Na Moon-hee Choi Woo-sung)

12
00:02:28.665 --> 00:02:32.632
(My Perfect Roommate)

13
00:02:48.899 --> 00:02:50.685
Don't drag your suitcase.

14
00:02:50.765 --> 00:02:52.199
I just wiped the floor.

15
00:03:21.199 --> 00:03:26.152
And this is really important.

16
00:03:26.232 --> 00:03:29.032
I'm feeling sorry to tell you but.

17
00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:31.399
Anything else?

18
00:03:32.832 --> 00:03:35.152
Please don't poo at home.

19
00:03:35.232 --> 00:03:37.432
(Defecation not allowed)

20
00:03:40.965 --> 00:03:42.725
I just can't imagine

21
00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:44.785
sharing the toilet with a man.

22
00:03:44.865 --> 00:03:47.152
I've lived alone all my life.

23
00:03:47.232 --> 00:03:48.685
I'm sorry.

24
00:03:48.765 --> 00:03:49.765
Sure.

25
00:04:11.699 --> 00:04:15.752
(Room Sharing
between elderly and student)

26
00:04:15.832 --> 00:04:17.099
Grandchildren,
my ass…

27
00:04:30.565 --> 00:04:32.119
Look at this.

28
00:04:32.199 --> 00:04:34.019
Grandmother knows the art.

29
00:04:34.099 --> 00:04:36.919
Living room looks
like Mondrian's job.

30
00:04:36.999 --> 00:04:39.352
Shut up.
Seriously,

31
00:04:39.432 --> 00:04:41.185
How can you live like this?

32
00:04:41.265 --> 00:04:43.232
Ask another place
to the city hall.

33
00:04:45.165 --> 00:04:47.785
- Do you see the main gate?
- Yes.

34
00:04:47.865 --> 00:04:49.545
People queues about that far
to replace me.

35
00:04:50.099 --> 00:04:51.385
Really?

36
00:04:51.465 --> 00:04:53.265
So it's cheaper than a studio?

37
00:04:53.765 --> 00:04:55.752
It has a window,
twice bigger but cheaper.

38
00:04:55.832 --> 00:04:57.699
I have no choice.

39
00:04:58.399 --> 00:05:00.199
You silver spoon knows nothing.

40
00:05:02.832 --> 00:05:05.619
Would you stop laughing?

41
00:05:05.699 --> 00:05:07.005
It's so funny

42
00:05:07.085 --> 00:05:08.786
that you can't poo at home.

43
00:05:10.073 --> 00:05:11.299
Whatever.

44
00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:12.608
I have to dig
with my dirt spoon.

45
00:05:12.632 --> 00:05:13.665
Again?

46
00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:16.075
I need at least $600 per month
just for breathing.

47
00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:17.585
Will you give it to me?

48
00:05:17.665 --> 00:05:19.719
- Don't cross the line.
- That's why I'm leaving.

49
00:05:19.799 --> 00:05:21.999
Wait for me.

50
00:05:23.199 --> 00:05:24.751
You work 5 days in a week.

51
00:05:24.831 --> 00:05:26.865
It's a weekend, don't go.

52
00:05:29.265 --> 00:05:30.387
He's been there over 3 months.

53
00:05:30.411 --> 00:05:33.185
I thought someone lives there.

54
00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.765
- I had no idea.
- Tell me about it.

55
00:06:16.632 --> 00:06:19.152
(Please use it
for cleaning my room I'm sorry)

56
00:06:19.232 --> 00:06:20.765
(Contact Son Kim Du Hong)

57
00:07:31.532 --> 00:07:33.099
- Bye.
- Thanks.

58
00:07:36.399 --> 00:07:39.343
Can't use the toilet at home

59
00:07:39.423 --> 00:07:40.432
makes my stomach nervous.

60
00:07:40.832 --> 00:07:42.285
Should've chosen a different menu?

61
00:07:42.365 --> 00:07:43.799
No, I can run fast enough.

62
00:07:45.599 --> 00:07:47.652
- Here.
- Thanks!

63
00:07:47.732 --> 00:07:48.985
How is he?

64
00:07:49.065 --> 00:07:50.485
What?

65
00:07:50.565 --> 00:07:52.085
Dae Hun.

66
00:07:52.165 --> 00:07:53.265
Still shows up?

67
00:07:54.365 --> 00:07:55.765
Not recently.

68
00:07:56.999 --> 00:07:59.952
If he asks money, say no.

69
00:08:00.032 --> 00:08:01.765
When will he come to his senses?

70
00:08:02.232 --> 00:08:03.232
Don't worry.

71
00:08:04.165 --> 00:08:06.485
All right,
I'll call you on the next job.

72
00:08:06.565 --> 00:08:09.032
- Okay.
- You must be tired, go home.

73
00:08:10.465 --> 00:08:12.385
- Safe drive!
- Okay.

74
00:08:12.465 --> 00:08:14.865
You must be tired then me,
it's a long drive.

75
00:08:36.365 --> 00:08:37.552
Something's wrong?

76
00:08:37.632 --> 00:08:39.037
The common area

77
00:08:39.117 --> 00:08:40.365
must be cleaned together.

78
00:08:45.099 --> 00:08:47.765
(Cleaning Roster)

79
00:08:49.732 --> 00:08:51.652
As I said, don't cross the red.

80
00:08:51.732 --> 00:08:54.152
Clean the yellow and blue areas.

81
00:08:54.232 --> 00:08:57.165
Okay.

82
00:09:22.265 --> 00:09:23.545
Clean the bathroom,

83
00:09:23.625 --> 00:09:24.632
it's your day off.

84
00:09:25.599 --> 00:09:27.319
Okay.

85
00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:28.832
Give me a moment.

86
00:09:32.232 --> 00:09:33.265
What's wrong?

87
00:09:55.565 --> 00:09:57.685
Why do you go to the toilet
so often?

88
00:09:57.765 --> 00:09:59.985
I have irritable bowel syndrome.

89
00:10:00.065 --> 00:10:01.299
Irritable...
what?

90
00:10:02.499 --> 00:10:04.757
Under the stress

91
00:10:04.837 --> 00:10:06.352
or psychological pressure.

92
00:10:06.432 --> 00:10:08.252
It's an incurable.

93
00:10:08.332 --> 00:10:10.632
I guess I was so stressed out
in the morning.

94
00:10:12.299 --> 00:10:13.427
It's so obvious

95
00:10:13.507 --> 00:10:14.507
you don't want to clean.

96
00:10:14.532 --> 00:10:15.699
Clean the bathroom!

97
00:10:26.432 --> 00:10:28.152
Turn the lever to the cold.

98
00:10:28.232 --> 00:10:29.865
Otherwise,
the boiler will keep running.

99
00:10:36.999 --> 00:10:39.552
Thank you
for cleaning this morning.

100
00:10:39.632 --> 00:10:41.160
You must be hungry

101
00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.919
going to the toilet so often.

102
00:10:42.999 --> 00:10:44.452
Have a breakfast.

103
00:10:44.532 --> 00:10:45.941
I'm fine,
I can go to the convenience store.

104
00:10:45.965 --> 00:10:47.832
Come on, sit down.

105
00:10:52.432 --> 00:10:53.465
Try it.

106
00:10:54.565 --> 00:10:55.565
Okay, then.

107
00:10:55.598 --> 00:10:56.598
If you skip the meal,

108
00:10:56.632 --> 00:10:58.565
you will suffer when you're old.

109
00:10:59.665 --> 00:11:01.165
How do you eat usually?

110
00:11:02.132 --> 00:11:04.185
At a convenience store
or school cafeteria.

111
00:11:04.265 --> 00:11:05.319
It's cheap.

112
00:11:05.399 --> 00:11:08.552
How much do you spend
at a convenience store?

113
00:11:08.632 --> 00:11:11.119
Gimbap, cup ramen...
About 4 dollars?

114
00:11:11.199 --> 00:11:12.385
Right?

115
00:11:12.465 --> 00:11:15.485
I'll make a proper meal for 5.

116
00:11:15.565 --> 00:11:16.485
What?

117
00:11:16.565 --> 00:11:18.785
Can you compare it to ramen?

118
00:11:18.865 --> 00:11:21.352
You can try it today
and tell me.

119
00:11:21.432 --> 00:11:24.952
Why would you eat outside
if you can eat at home?

120
00:11:25.032 --> 00:11:28.385
How is it?
5 is cheap, right?

121
00:11:28.465 --> 00:11:30.099
The first day,
it's on the house.

122
00:11:56.065 --> 00:11:58.152
(Soup run for the elders)

123
00:11:58.232 --> 00:11:59.952
Sorry, I'm late.
Traffic was so heavy.

124
00:12:00.032 --> 00:12:01.365
Enjoy your meal!

125
00:12:04.365 --> 00:12:05.365
Enjoy your meal!

126
00:12:06.532 --> 00:12:07.665
Enjoy your meal!

127
00:12:12.565 --> 00:12:13.785
Mrs!

128
00:12:13.865 --> 00:12:16.252
It's for my friend coming late!

129
00:12:16.332 --> 00:12:17.952
Still no.

130
00:12:18.032 --> 00:12:19.893
Some people are late.

131
00:12:19.973 --> 00:12:21.465
Why not?

132
00:12:25.099 --> 00:12:26.365
Enjoy your meal.

133
00:12:56.432 --> 00:12:59.152
Mrs, you took the medicine
a few days ago.

134
00:12:59.232 --> 00:13:00.685
My whole body aches.

135
00:13:00.765 --> 00:13:03.665
Every part hurts
when someone touches me.

136
00:13:06.465 --> 00:13:07.732
Press here.

137
00:13:11.265 --> 00:13:14.019
I said press it, not poke!

138
00:13:14.099 --> 00:13:15.685
It hurts so much.

139
00:13:15.765 --> 00:13:17.232
Give me my prescription.

140
00:13:17.865 --> 00:13:19.919
If you keep doing this,

141
00:13:19.999 --> 00:13:23.232
there will be not enough medicine
for others.

142
00:13:32.599 --> 00:13:33.719
What's your schedule today?

143
00:13:33.799 --> 00:13:35.519
Shall we go to the movie?

144
00:13:35.599 --> 00:13:37.319
Shall we?

145
00:13:37.399 --> 00:13:39.519
Call?
Okay.

146
00:13:39.599 --> 00:13:41.019
I'll buy tickets now.

147
00:13:41.099 --> 00:13:43.752
Meals on you, drinks on me!

148
00:13:43.832 --> 00:13:45.285
- Call?
- Call!

149
00:13:45.365 --> 00:13:46.865
Okay!

150
00:13:56.132 --> 00:13:57.132
It's mine.

151
00:13:57.432 --> 00:13:59.065
Hello?

152
00:13:59.599 --> 00:14:01.632
Hi, yes.

153
00:14:02.532 --> 00:14:04.232
For three days?

154
00:14:06.732 --> 00:14:10.032
No, it's not because of money.

155
00:14:10.865 --> 00:14:14.465
Yes, I got it.
Bye.

156
00:14:16.765 --> 00:14:17.765
What is it?

157
00:14:18.632 --> 00:14:20.652
It's a pet sitting job.

158
00:14:20.732 --> 00:14:21.852
They're having an emergency,

159
00:14:21.932 --> 00:14:23.608
need me to take the puppy

160
00:14:23.688 --> 00:14:25.085
for three days.

161
00:14:25.165 --> 00:14:28.052
I already bought tickets,
you should've said no.

162
00:14:28.132 --> 00:14:31.085
And…
You don't have a house.

163
00:14:31.165 --> 00:14:32.585
I know!

164
00:14:32.665 --> 00:14:34.665
But she's one of my
very few regular customers.

165
00:14:35.665 --> 00:14:37.919
But you just started.

166
00:14:37.999 --> 00:14:39.852
That makes me more thankful.

167
00:14:39.932 --> 00:14:41.385
What should I do?

168
00:14:41.465 --> 00:14:43.185
Call her back, say you can't!

169
00:14:43.265 --> 00:14:44.652
Let's go to the theater!

170
00:14:44.732 --> 00:14:47.685
Her mom had an accident,
she has to take care of her!

171
00:14:47.765 --> 00:14:50.485
Let's go!
Hey! Come on.

172
00:14:50.565 --> 00:14:52.432
I won't go either.

173
00:15:35.932 --> 00:15:38.319
Hello, I'm Han Ji Woong.

174
00:15:38.399 --> 00:15:39.985
I'm sorry.
Am I late?

175
00:15:40.065 --> 00:15:41.152
No, you're on time.

176
00:15:41.232 --> 00:15:42.885
I'm sorry for such short notice.

177
00:15:42.965 --> 00:15:45.578
My mom hurt her leg

178
00:15:45.658 --> 00:15:47.209
but my dad is on a business trip.

179
00:15:47.289 --> 00:15:49.352
My dad told me
he hired you once before.

180
00:15:49.432 --> 00:15:51.732
Yes.
Hi Jing! Come here!

181
00:15:54.532 --> 00:15:55.741
Thank you.

182
00:15:55.821 --> 00:15:57.252
Don't worry, go ahead.

183
00:16:08.199 --> 00:16:09.665
What should we do?

184
00:16:19.799 --> 00:16:22.252
201!

185
00:16:22.332 --> 00:16:23.799
Have some corns.

186
00:16:28.765 --> 00:16:29.919
I guess she's busy.

187
00:16:29.999 --> 00:16:31.999
Why would you call her
who won't even come?

188
00:16:32.532 --> 00:16:35.485
She's about to meet
her husband in heaven.

189
00:16:35.565 --> 00:16:37.365
How could she always be so cold?

190
00:16:38.132 --> 00:16:39.657
Do you still want to meet
your husband

191
00:16:39.737 --> 00:16:41.219
in the afterlife?

192
00:16:41.299 --> 00:16:42.952
There will be
a lot of other men!

193
00:16:43.032 --> 00:16:45.232
Look at her,
she can't hold her smile.

194
00:16:53.665 --> 00:16:54.719
Why are we walking?

195
00:16:54.799 --> 00:16:56.919
Not going home?

196
00:16:56.999 --> 00:16:58.252
Actually, I...

197
00:16:58.332 --> 00:17:00.985
I'm living
with a scary old lady.

198
00:17:01.065 --> 00:17:03.132
If she sees you,
we might be kicked out!

199
00:17:09.665 --> 00:17:10.865
Jing!
Let's help her.

200
00:17:18.799 --> 00:17:19.865
Almost there!

201
00:17:22.165 --> 00:17:23.465
Jing!
Stay put.

202
00:18:20.265 --> 00:18:21.485
Be quiet!

203
00:18:21.565 --> 00:18:23.932
I told you what's going on.

204
00:18:26.099 --> 00:18:28.619
Come on, shut up!

205
00:18:28.699 --> 00:18:30.399
I heard a dog barking.

206
00:18:32.532 --> 00:18:33.799
What are you doing outside?

207
00:18:34.965 --> 00:18:37.119
It's nothing.

208
00:18:37.199 --> 00:18:38.599
What's that sound?

209
00:18:47.432 --> 00:18:49.032
Please, only for three days.

210
00:18:50.932 --> 00:18:52.699
So you brought the dog?

211
00:18:53.232 --> 00:18:55.552
- Yes.
- What nonsense is this?

212
00:18:55.632 --> 00:18:57.385
At my house,
without my permission!

213
00:18:57.465 --> 00:18:58.785
The owner needed help…

214
00:18:58.865 --> 00:19:00.119
How about me?

215
00:19:00.199 --> 00:19:01.919
I don't even like human being.

216
00:19:01.999 --> 00:19:03.794
But a dog?

217
00:19:03.874 --> 00:19:05.785
- For three days?
- I'm sorry.

218
00:19:05.865 --> 00:19:09.019
No.
Never.

219
00:19:09.099 --> 00:19:11.119
Hairs will be everywhere!

220
00:19:11.199 --> 00:19:13.352
I can't eat if I see one.

221
00:19:13.432 --> 00:19:15.985
I will clean by myself
for the next week.

222
00:19:16.065 --> 00:19:17.453
And the dishes!

223
00:19:17.533 --> 00:19:18.785
Besides…

224
00:19:18.865 --> 00:19:19.919
What about pee and poo?

225
00:19:19.999 --> 00:19:21.721
He pees at the bathroom,

226
00:19:21.801 --> 00:19:22.828
hoes little water on…

227
00:19:22.908 --> 00:19:24.285
It will smell!

228
00:19:24.365 --> 00:19:25.675
Bathroom cleaning
for the whole week!

229
00:19:25.699 --> 00:19:26.699
I mean, the whole month!

230
00:19:26.732 --> 00:19:28.019
What about poo?

231
00:19:28.099 --> 00:19:30.119
He's really smart,
poops only outside.

232
00:19:30.199 --> 00:19:32.652
I will take him out
after school.

233
00:19:32.732 --> 00:19:35.052
How about
when you're not around?

234
00:19:35.132 --> 00:19:36.499
I'll take him with me.

235
00:19:40.765 --> 00:19:43.219
You know you're being illogical.

236
00:19:43.299 --> 00:19:44.385
Yes.

237
00:19:44.465 --> 00:19:47.719
But the owner's mom
had a car accident…

238
00:19:47.799 --> 00:19:48.852
Young man.

239
00:19:48.932 --> 00:19:50.985
If you look
after someone else's life,

240
00:19:51.065 --> 00:19:54.252
your life will be miserable.

241
00:19:54.332 --> 00:19:55.585
Even so,

242
00:19:55.665 --> 00:19:59.452
We must help each other
in this society.

243
00:19:59.532 --> 00:20:00.685
What?

244
00:20:00.765 --> 00:20:02.685
We all living together.

245
00:20:02.765 --> 00:20:06.619
People always need
someone's help.

246
00:20:06.699 --> 00:20:08.217
Are you showing off

247
00:20:08.297 --> 00:20:09.185
that you're majoring in sociology?

248
00:20:09.265 --> 00:20:12.332
No, I'm not.
It's my personality.

249
00:20:15.032 --> 00:20:16.665
7:3

250
00:20:17.299 --> 00:20:18.652
No, it's my house,
and obviously,

251
00:20:18.732 --> 00:20:20.732
I take care of him
in the daytime.

252
00:20:21.765 --> 00:20:22.852
What?

253
00:20:22.932 --> 00:20:24.919
8:2

254
00:20:24.999 --> 00:20:28.552
But Mrs,
that's unfair…

255
00:20:28.632 --> 00:20:30.285
9:1?

256
00:20:30.365 --> 00:20:35.085
No, 8:2.
Of course, it is.

257
00:20:35.165 --> 00:20:36.865
Thank you.

258
00:20:38.832 --> 00:20:40.132
7:3

259
00:20:41.599 --> 00:20:43.485
Deposit it into my bank account.

260
00:20:43.565 --> 00:20:45.752
The contract is established.

261
00:20:45.832 --> 00:20:47.885
Call?

262
00:20:47.965 --> 00:20:49.099
Yes, I call.

263
00:21:18.099 --> 00:21:21.052
Putting so much effort into it.

264
00:21:21.132 --> 00:21:22.585
Do that to your parents.

265
00:21:22.665 --> 00:21:24.832
They'll carry you around
as a good son.

266
00:21:25.632 --> 00:21:27.232
You pay
for electricity this month.

267
00:21:29.499 --> 00:21:30.665
Okay.

268
00:21:35.499 --> 00:21:37.585
Don't give him anything else.

269
00:21:37.665 --> 00:21:40.619
Only this jerky for a snack.

270
00:21:40.699 --> 00:21:42.819
I've heard enough!

271
00:21:42.899 --> 00:21:43.961
Go,

272
00:21:44.041 --> 00:21:46.885
or I'll lock the door
and leave him outside.

273
00:21:46.965 --> 00:21:48.419
I'll be back in hurry.

274
00:21:48.499 --> 00:21:51.885
I'll be off to school.

275
00:21:51.965 --> 00:21:54.597
Jing! Brother will be back.

276
00:21:54.677 --> 00:21:56.099
Behave yourself!

277
00:21:57.865 --> 00:22:00.199
Brother my ass…
To the dog.

278
00:22:02.432 --> 00:22:03.465
See you later.

279
00:22:15.099 --> 00:22:16.399
- Seriously?
- Yes.

280
00:22:17.299 --> 00:22:19.332
- She let you?
- Yes.

281
00:22:20.432 --> 00:22:23.699
That's unbelievable.
What's in it for you?

282
00:22:25.465 --> 00:22:26.752
Nothing.

283
00:22:26.832 --> 00:22:29.485
Come on, I can feel it.

284
00:22:29.565 --> 00:22:31.399
There's nothing.

285
00:22:31.965 --> 00:22:34.985
You have many flaws
but generosity is the worst.

286
00:22:35.065 --> 00:22:37.299
That's why we're still friends.

287
00:22:43.332 --> 00:22:44.372
Coffee bet!
5 points first!

288
00:22:48.365 --> 00:22:50.065
- One to nothing.
- Okay, one to zero.

289
00:22:58.399 --> 00:23:00.432
You're no match for me.

290
00:23:50.899 --> 00:23:52.452
Hello.

291
00:23:52.532 --> 00:23:54.419
Do you live 201?

292
00:23:54.499 --> 00:23:56.352
I'm friend of Gum Bun.

293
00:23:56.432 --> 00:23:59.352
Hello.

294
00:23:59.432 --> 00:24:00.052
Hyung Seok.

295
00:24:00.132 --> 00:24:03.085
He's a student living
with grandmother of 201.

296
00:24:03.165 --> 00:24:06.985
Nice to meet you,
I'm Seo Hyung Seok.

297
00:24:07.065 --> 00:24:09.119
- Hi.
- It's hard, right?

298
00:24:09.199 --> 00:24:10.932
Living with a cranky grandmother.

299
00:24:12.232 --> 00:24:13.385
It's okay.

300
00:24:13.465 --> 00:24:16.499
Please open up a little bit
young man!

301
00:24:19.099 --> 00:24:23.052
I'm going to watch movie
with him.

302
00:24:23.132 --> 00:24:25.765
- Have a good time.
- See you again.

303
00:24:27.865 --> 00:24:30.385
What do you want
to eat after movie?

304
00:24:30.465 --> 00:24:32.899
Let's eat something delicious
for dinner.

305
00:24:39.665 --> 00:24:41.385
Fetch!

306
00:24:41.465 --> 00:24:43.119
Good boy.
Come on.

307
00:24:43.199 --> 00:24:46.152
Good boy.
Here you go.

308
00:24:46.232 --> 00:24:48.365
(Jing's sister)

309
00:25:04.099 --> 00:25:07.865
Play with this!

310
00:25:09.165 --> 00:25:11.219
What's this?

311
00:25:11.299 --> 00:25:12.419
What is it?

312
00:25:12.499 --> 00:25:14.652
- It's a duck bone!
- What a waste.

313
00:25:14.732 --> 00:25:17.365
Toys, Snacks!
Better than person!

314
00:25:19.065 --> 00:25:20.385
So cute isn't he?

315
00:25:20.465 --> 00:25:22.219
Just like human,

316
00:25:22.299 --> 00:25:24.819
give him a love,
he'll love you back.

317
00:25:24.899 --> 00:25:27.232
Having fun?

318
00:25:30.632 --> 00:25:32.119
I'm going to the school.

319
00:25:32.199 --> 00:25:33.399
Please take care of him.

320
00:25:56.765 --> 00:25:59.185
Jing?

321
00:25:59.265 --> 00:26:01.332
It suits you.

322
00:26:06.732 --> 00:26:08.165
Do you like me?

323
00:26:24.132 --> 00:26:25.132
Where are you going?

324
00:26:25.199 --> 00:26:26.965
Walking,
it helps me digest better.

325
00:26:43.199 --> 00:26:45.052
Why are you following me around?

326
00:26:45.132 --> 00:26:46.207
The road looks good

327
00:26:46.287 --> 00:26:47.699
to walk for Jing.

328
00:27:06.132 --> 00:27:07.885
Leaving?

329
00:27:07.965 --> 00:27:09.245
Say goodbye
to grandmother, Jing!

330
00:27:10.199 --> 00:27:15.519
I'm glad he's leaving.

331
00:27:15.599 --> 00:27:18.399
I'm sick of hairs,
piss and poops.

332
00:28:05.599 --> 00:28:07.799
Put you down?

333
00:28:08.699 --> 00:28:11.485
Go to your sister.

334
00:28:11.565 --> 00:28:12.565
Go on.

335
00:28:14.065 --> 00:28:19.819
Did you miss me?

336
00:28:19.899 --> 00:28:21.032
Good boy.

337
00:28:21.665 --> 00:28:23.013
Thank you,

338
00:28:23.093 --> 00:28:24.785
such a short notice.

339
00:28:24.865 --> 00:28:26.019
How's your mom?

340
00:28:26.099 --> 00:28:29.452
It wasn't a big accident
but she hurts her leg.

341
00:28:29.532 --> 00:28:31.565
That's a relief.

342
00:28:35.132 --> 00:28:36.919
This is his toy.

343
00:28:36.999 --> 00:28:38.530
The old one was a little hard

344
00:28:38.610 --> 00:28:40.885
for his soft gum.

345
00:28:40.965 --> 00:28:44.519
These are jerkies I made.

346
00:28:44.599 --> 00:28:46.785
He is a little rascal,

347
00:28:46.865 --> 00:28:48.534
toys will help him

348
00:28:48.614 --> 00:28:49.952
stop chewing things.

349
00:28:50.032 --> 00:28:52.185
Give him a duck bone after toy.

350
00:28:52.265 --> 00:28:53.341
That's a relief.
For 3 days.

351
00:28:53.365 --> 00:28:55.385
He'll get better.

352
00:28:55.465 --> 00:28:57.379
Thank you,

353
00:28:57.459 --> 00:29:01.419
I was having a hard time.

354
00:29:01.499 --> 00:29:03.551
Can I ask you sometimes?

355
00:29:03.631 --> 00:29:06.885
He's my first pet.

356
00:29:06.965 --> 00:29:09.099
Of course, if it helps you.

357
00:29:40.132 --> 00:29:43.119
Are you leaving too?

358
00:29:43.199 --> 00:29:45.165
Go away, all of you.

359
00:29:48.732 --> 00:29:50.665
So, have you decided
on your washing machine?

360
00:29:52.365 --> 00:29:54.152
Well…

361
00:29:54.232 --> 00:29:56.552
Anything I can afford.

362
00:29:56.632 --> 00:29:58.919
You used it long enough.

363
00:29:58.999 --> 00:30:02.265
Must throw something away
to get new in.

364
00:30:04.265 --> 00:30:07.285
- Do you want me to drive?
- No, it's fine.

365
00:30:07.365 --> 00:30:09.965
I don't want
to frighten the car.

366
00:30:12.565 --> 00:30:13.819
(Every Tuesday
$2.5 for noodles)

367
00:30:13.899 --> 00:30:17.087
- Welcome. Please have a seat.
- Let's sit here.

368
00:30:18.999 --> 00:30:20.439
Two black-bean-sauce noodles,
please.

369
00:30:22.665 --> 00:30:23.965
Two noodles coming right up.

370
00:30:25.832 --> 00:30:28.619
It's on me, help yourself.

371
00:30:28.699 --> 00:30:30.213
No, you helped me

372
00:30:30.293 --> 00:30:31.852
buying washing machine.

373
00:30:31.932 --> 00:30:35.385
Don't be, If a person changes,
it's time to die.

374
00:30:35.465 --> 00:30:38.242
If you go before me

375
00:30:38.322 --> 00:30:39.929
after buying this cheap noodle,

376
00:30:40.009 --> 00:30:41.419
it'll remain
in my heart forever.

377
00:30:41.499 --> 00:30:43.465
It's on me.

378
00:30:47.132 --> 00:30:48.852
What do you think?
It's nice, right?

379
00:30:48.932 --> 00:30:50.432
Having someone around.

380
00:30:52.299 --> 00:30:53.532
Well…

381
00:30:56.432 --> 00:30:58.919
My boy has to join the military.

382
00:30:58.999 --> 00:31:02.232
Breaks my heart.

383
00:31:03.632 --> 00:31:07.152
Your boy looks great.

384
00:31:07.232 --> 00:31:08.799
Be nice to him.

385
00:31:14.499 --> 00:31:16.328
I like him

386
00:31:16.891 --> 00:31:19.719
because he feels like my grandson.

387
00:31:19.799 --> 00:31:22.332
How friendly he is.

388
00:31:30.432 --> 00:31:32.132
(Modern Sociology)

389
00:31:42.765 --> 00:31:43.765
(Jing's sister)

390
00:31:43.799 --> 00:31:46.565
He barks to every sound
from the door.

391
00:31:49.165 --> 00:31:51.119
I think it's time to socialize.

392
00:31:51.199 --> 00:31:55.952
The vet said
that this is an important time.

393
00:31:56.032 --> 00:31:57.519
What should I do?

394
00:31:57.599 --> 00:31:59.065
How about this?

395
00:32:22.265 --> 00:32:23.265
What's this?

396
00:32:25.532 --> 00:32:28.565
Are you trying
to impress someone?

397
00:32:31.832 --> 00:32:32.832
Do you have a blind date?

398
00:32:42.965 --> 00:32:44.999
- Here are your beers.
- Thank you.

399
00:32:48.199 --> 00:32:55.565
Are you having a fun
with your friends?

400
00:32:59.632 --> 00:33:00.876
I've been to pet cafe,

401
00:33:00.956 --> 00:33:02.352
but didn't know a pet pub.

402
00:33:02.432 --> 00:33:04.119
Pets are a family.

403
00:33:04.199 --> 00:33:05.952
It's popular among pet owners.

404
00:33:06.032 --> 00:33:07.552
I love it.

405
00:33:07.632 --> 00:33:09.432
You are a good pet sitter,
Ji Woong.

406
00:33:12.899 --> 00:33:14.032
What?

407
00:33:14.665 --> 00:33:15.732
Spam.

408
00:33:17.065 --> 00:33:18.848
So we're at the same age,

409
00:33:18.928 --> 00:33:20.885
shall we talk comfortably?

410
00:33:20.965 --> 00:33:23.185
Shall we?

411
00:33:23.265 --> 00:33:25.319
- Absolutely.
- Choi Sung Jin.

412
00:33:25.399 --> 00:33:28.485
Didn't you say
about meeting someone?

413
00:33:28.565 --> 00:33:29.863
He kept following me

414
00:33:29.943 --> 00:33:31.852
saying he had an appointment!

415
00:33:31.932 --> 00:33:33.585
Why do you speak
in honorifics again?

416
00:33:33.665 --> 00:33:35.632
It's none of your business.

417
00:33:36.832 --> 00:33:39.285
I've never seen him
putting a hair wax.

418
00:33:39.365 --> 00:33:42.052
- Whatever.
- Look at your hair.

419
00:33:42.132 --> 00:33:44.319
Shut up, don't listen to him.

420
00:33:44.399 --> 00:33:45.776
Now we're friends,

421
00:33:45.856 --> 00:33:48.085
I can ask about Jing easily.

422
00:33:48.165 --> 00:33:51.332
Right?
Right? Jing?

423
00:33:52.199 --> 00:33:53.632
Do you want a snack?

424
00:34:31.832 --> 00:34:35.065
(Women's restroom)

425
00:35:20.665 --> 00:35:21.552
Try this yogurt.

426
00:35:21.632 --> 00:35:23.219
Now we're friends,

427
00:35:23.299 --> 00:35:26.799
I always get support from you.

428
00:35:27.432 --> 00:35:28.969
There're no boxes today.

429
00:35:29.049 --> 00:35:31.332
Really? I put them outside.

430
00:35:31.532 --> 00:35:32.932
Okay.

431
00:35:41.032 --> 00:35:42.685
It's you again, old man?

432
00:35:42.765 --> 00:35:45.285
Don't touch
other people's properties!

433
00:35:45.365 --> 00:35:47.619
- What properties?
- Look.

434
00:35:47.699 --> 00:35:49.785
This is my jurisdiction.

435
00:35:49.865 --> 00:35:51.586
Where is your manner?

436
00:35:51.666 --> 00:35:52.666
This is theft!

437
00:35:52.732 --> 00:35:54.310
I left for a few days

438
00:35:54.390 --> 00:35:56.285
but you cant take my boxes!

439
00:35:56.365 --> 00:35:58.885
They were on the road,
first come, first serve!

440
00:35:58.965 --> 00:36:00.952
Look!
These are from the pizza place,

441
00:36:01.032 --> 00:36:03.185
These are
from the chicken place.

442
00:36:03.265 --> 00:36:05.519
Did I ever take yours?

443
00:36:05.599 --> 00:36:07.652
I don't even look at them.

444
00:36:07.732 --> 00:36:10.819
Stay away from my street!

445
00:36:10.899 --> 00:36:12.285
Spiteful, venomous.

446
00:36:12.365 --> 00:36:15.665
What a grumpy old woman.

447
00:36:40.699 --> 00:36:43.199
Great job.

448
00:36:45.532 --> 00:36:52.285
Here is your $12, wait.

449
00:36:52.365 --> 00:36:53.999
Here, $12 and 30 cents total.

450
00:36:55.732 --> 00:36:57.252
It's getting less.

451
00:36:57.332 --> 00:37:00.785
It's a hard time.

452
00:37:00.865 --> 00:37:04.485
The price keeps going down lately.
It's crazy.

453
00:37:04.565 --> 00:37:08.265
I know.
The world is getting harder.

454
00:37:09.299 --> 00:37:11.265
But what can we do?
Life goes on!

455
00:37:13.632 --> 00:37:15.499
- Take care.
- See you later.

456
00:37:21.932 --> 00:37:26.685
I was so stressed out preparing
Scholastic Aptitude Test.

457
00:37:26.765 --> 00:37:29.919
Mom nagged
"Do you think that's enough?"

458
00:37:29.999 --> 00:37:32.919
"You'll have fun
at the university."

459
00:37:32.999 --> 00:37:35.319
She was sugarcoating it.

460
00:37:35.399 --> 00:37:38.319
She exactly sounds like my mom.

461
00:37:38.399 --> 00:37:41.885
How about you?

462
00:37:41.965 --> 00:37:44.380
I bet your parents were different

463
00:37:44.460 --> 00:37:46.632
seeing you live so hard.

464
00:37:47.632 --> 00:37:51.119
My family?

465
00:37:51.199 --> 00:37:52.832
No, just the same.

466
00:37:55.132 --> 00:37:57.052
They just try
to take care of you.

467
00:37:57.132 --> 00:37:59.585
My dad calls me
every day at 10 p.m.

468
00:37:59.665 --> 00:38:02.799
Dad, just let me have some fun.

469
00:38:06.432 --> 00:38:08.755
And that's my mom.

470
00:38:08.835 --> 00:38:11.719
She's like a cuckoo clock.

471
00:38:11.799 --> 00:38:13.999
Hey,
I wish I can live alone like you.

472
00:38:36.599 --> 00:38:38.165
Where have you been?

473
00:38:39.865 --> 00:38:41.432
Out of cooking oil.

474
00:38:42.132 --> 00:38:43.132
Dinner?

475
00:38:44.265 --> 00:38:45.365
Soon.

476
00:38:47.365 --> 00:38:48.865
Where's everyone?

477
00:38:49.465 --> 00:38:56.452
806 went home with her son,

478
00:38:56.532 --> 00:39:00.499
301 has to put her grandson
to sleep.

479
00:39:00.899 --> 00:39:02.852
You tell your son
and grandchild to come.

480
00:39:02.932 --> 00:39:04.765
You miss them all the time!

481
00:39:06.699 --> 00:39:09.685
Few days ago, at dawn,

482
00:39:09.765 --> 00:39:14.285
I was so sick
that I couldn't move.

483
00:39:14.365 --> 00:39:15.919
So I was struggling alone,

484
00:39:15.999 --> 00:39:17.833
then I called my son telling him

485
00:39:18.380 --> 00:39:22.719
to take me to the hospital.

486
00:39:22.799 --> 00:39:27.685
After a while, a doorbell rang.

487
00:39:27.765 --> 00:39:30.052
So I opened the door.

488
00:39:30.132 --> 00:39:31.632
It was a damn ambulance.

489
00:39:32.832 --> 00:39:35.352
My son called 911.

490
00:39:35.432 --> 00:39:38.032
To take me to the hospital.

491
00:39:40.132 --> 00:39:43.452
I understand.

492
00:39:43.532 --> 00:39:46.152
He's busy living his life but...

493
00:39:46.232 --> 00:39:47.472
But he gives you a lot of money.

494
00:39:48.265 --> 00:39:50.052
Money can't replace everything.

495
00:39:50.132 --> 00:39:51.519
Count your blessing.

496
00:39:51.599 --> 00:39:55.685
He gives you money,
calls the ambulance.

497
00:39:55.765 --> 00:39:57.985
That's enough!

498
00:39:58.065 --> 00:40:01.019
I can't listen
to your bragging anymore.

499
00:40:01.099 --> 00:40:03.285
What a temper.

500
00:40:03.365 --> 00:40:06.185
I was about to go inside.

501
00:40:06.265 --> 00:40:07.599
Wait for me!

502
00:40:39.365 --> 00:40:40.499
Brother.

503
00:40:41.832 --> 00:40:43.385
How did you find me?

504
00:40:43.465 --> 00:40:46.865
I'm nosy, I asked around.

505
00:40:47.399 --> 00:40:49.774
It's been a while,

506
00:40:49.854 --> 00:40:52.252
be nice to your friend.

507
00:40:52.332 --> 00:40:53.719
I'm totally broke.

508
00:40:53.799 --> 00:40:55.485
It's not like that.

509
00:40:55.565 --> 00:40:58.632
I came to see your face
on the way to Min Chul.

510
00:40:59.232 --> 00:41:01.785
- Really?
- Yes, you punk.

511
00:41:01.865 --> 00:41:04.452
If I go there,
who knows when we meet again?

512
00:41:04.532 --> 00:41:05.752
Good for you.

513
00:41:05.832 --> 00:41:07.799
You'll save money
if you work for a while.

514
00:41:08.532 --> 00:41:11.752
Yeah, right.

515
00:41:11.832 --> 00:41:12.959
You could've told me

516
00:41:13.039 --> 00:41:14.319
you will be late on the phone.

517
00:41:14.399 --> 00:41:15.965
It was on silent mode.

518
00:41:17.265 --> 00:41:18.952
Look at you.

519
00:41:19.032 --> 00:41:20.519
You're dating someone?

520
00:41:20.599 --> 00:41:22.332
What dating?
No.

521
00:41:24.165 --> 00:41:26.952
Hey.
I'm too late today.

522
00:41:27.032 --> 00:41:28.952
Let's go to your place.

523
00:41:29.032 --> 00:41:31.752
No, grandmother hates it
when people come.

524
00:41:31.832 --> 00:41:33.919
Why?
I'm your friend.

525
00:41:33.999 --> 00:41:35.732
She just doesn't like it.

526
00:41:36.265 --> 00:41:37.519
All right, all right.

527
00:41:37.599 --> 00:41:39.532
Then I'll stay
until the first train.

528
00:42:05.832 --> 00:42:08.752
Ji Woong.
Reminds me the old time.

529
00:42:08.832 --> 00:42:10.532
Shut up.

530
00:42:16.899 --> 00:42:18.699
We still got it, dude.
Still the same.

531
00:42:25.665 --> 00:42:32.285
What kind of dog eats an apple?

532
00:42:32.365 --> 00:42:33.552
And pumpkins too?

533
00:42:33.632 --> 00:42:37.899
Sure, it can prevent constipation
and take vitamins.

534
00:42:41.232 --> 00:42:43.485
I envy you.

535
00:42:43.565 --> 00:42:45.347
You go to university in Seoul

536
00:42:45.427 --> 00:42:47.319
preparing for the future.

537
00:42:47.399 --> 00:42:51.519
You must work hard
for Min Chul for a year.

538
00:42:51.599 --> 00:42:52.899
All right, smartass.

539
00:43:19.699 --> 00:43:20.832
Who are you?

540
00:43:25.699 --> 00:43:26.699
I'm friend of Ji Woong.

541
00:43:26.765 --> 00:43:28.652
I'm sorry!
He was about to leave.

542
00:43:28.732 --> 00:43:30.019
What's wrong?

543
00:43:30.099 --> 00:43:31.285
Leave now.

544
00:43:31.365 --> 00:43:33.199
Before I call the police.

545
00:43:33.665 --> 00:43:36.432
What?
Why are you making a fuss?

546
00:43:36.932 --> 00:43:37.819
Let's go.

547
00:43:37.899 --> 00:43:39.529
Why? Call the police!

548
00:43:39.609 --> 00:43:40.785
Come on, let's go.

549
00:43:40.865 --> 00:43:42.719
She treats me like a criminal!

550
00:43:42.799 --> 00:43:44.799
Put on your shoes.
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

551
00:43:51.432 --> 00:43:52.732
I'll pay you back

552
00:43:52.812 --> 00:43:54.852
as soon as I get paid.

553
00:43:54.932 --> 00:43:57.099
I'm sorry.
This and that, too.

554
00:43:57.632 --> 00:43:58.932
Okay, go.

555
00:44:01.499 --> 00:44:02.632
See you later.

556
00:44:14.332 --> 00:44:15.432
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

557
00:44:18.365 --> 00:44:19.899
It was outrageous.

558
00:44:22.765 --> 00:44:24.185
I'm sorry.

559
00:44:24.265 --> 00:44:26.273
He acted like he has no parents,

560
00:44:26.353 --> 00:44:28.419
is he your friend?

561
00:44:28.499 --> 00:44:30.152
Please don't talk
too recklessly.

562
00:44:30.232 --> 00:44:34.219
Do you think he acted right?

563
00:44:34.299 --> 00:44:35.452
No, I don't.

564
00:44:35.532 --> 00:44:37.752
But all he did was
use the bathroom.

565
00:44:37.832 --> 00:44:40.619
He wandered around
a stranger's house!

566
00:44:40.699 --> 00:44:41.719
I know it's your house,

567
00:44:41.799 --> 00:44:44.352
but I'm living here too.

568
00:44:44.432 --> 00:44:45.785
What?

569
00:44:45.865 --> 00:44:47.628
What are you saying?

570
00:44:48.183 --> 00:44:49.952
What a thief!

571
00:44:50.032 --> 00:44:53.485
Now, your parents
must be so obvious!

572
00:44:53.565 --> 00:44:54.785
Ma'am!

573
00:44:54.865 --> 00:44:56.619
I'll give you a few days, leave.

574
00:44:56.699 --> 00:44:59.252
I can't live with someone
like you anymore!

575
00:44:59.332 --> 00:45:01.419
Yes, I will!

576
00:45:01.499 --> 00:45:04.319
Honestly, it was hard for me
to bear your personality.

577
00:45:04.399 --> 00:45:05.852
I can't wash
or defecate comfortably!

578
00:45:05.932 --> 00:45:07.385
How about eating?

579
00:45:07.465 --> 00:45:09.252
There aren't many people

580
00:45:09.332 --> 00:45:11.119
who can live with someone
like you!

581
00:45:11.199 --> 00:45:14.152
If it was that hard,
why did you hold it in?

582
00:45:14.232 --> 00:45:16.665
Fine!
That's good!

583
00:45:31.665 --> 00:45:33.619
What is today's job?

584
00:45:33.699 --> 00:45:34.785
Leave me alone.

585
00:45:34.865 --> 00:45:37.119
So cranky.

586
00:45:37.199 --> 00:45:39.085
Is it Yoo Jin?

587
00:45:39.165 --> 00:45:40.999
Get lost.

588
00:45:41.432 --> 00:45:43.219
Love is never easy.

589
00:45:43.299 --> 00:45:45.852
It requires infinite dedication
and patience,

590
00:45:45.932 --> 00:45:47.052
at last, there's love.

591
00:45:47.132 --> 00:45:48.852
You know nothing.

592
00:45:48.932 --> 00:45:50.552
Do I look so free to you?

593
00:45:50.632 --> 00:45:52.285
What kind of reaction is this?

594
00:45:52.365 --> 00:45:54.532
I saw you put a wax
on your hair.

595
00:45:55.099 --> 00:45:57.085
Come on, man.

596
00:45:57.165 --> 00:46:00.519
Let's freaking hang out!

597
00:46:00.599 --> 00:46:04.632
You've been an ass whole week.

598
00:46:07.099 --> 00:46:09.785
What?
What is it?

599
00:46:09.865 --> 00:46:11.485
I said get lost.

600
00:46:11.565 --> 00:46:12.685
Even if it's not you,

601
00:46:12.765 --> 00:46:14.165
I only have back tackles
in my life!

602
00:46:16.999 --> 00:46:18.365
Hey!

603
00:47:18.832 --> 00:47:22.265
What the hell she's doing?

604
00:47:23.632 --> 00:47:25.852
Get out of my way, old woman!

605
00:47:25.932 --> 00:47:29.265
Hold on.
I just need to pick this up.

606
00:47:44.599 --> 00:47:47.219
Are you deaf?
I'm busy!

607
00:47:47.299 --> 00:47:48.619
Almost done!

608
00:47:48.699 --> 00:47:51.332
Move!
I said move!

609
00:47:53.932 --> 00:47:55.765
Dammit!

610
00:48:04.832 --> 00:48:06.299
Come on!

611
00:48:22.999 --> 00:48:23.999
Grandmother?

612
00:48:25.632 --> 00:48:26.352
You!

613
00:48:26.432 --> 00:48:28.832
- Seriously…
- Hey, craphead!

614
00:48:32.632 --> 00:48:34.565
Who the hell are you?

615
00:48:35.232 --> 00:48:37.032
Who are you?

616
00:48:42.099 --> 00:48:44.385
What are you doing?

617
00:48:44.465 --> 00:48:48.499
What the heck are you doing?

618
00:48:54.765 --> 00:48:57.185
Crap, seriously.

619
00:48:57.265 --> 00:49:01.385
I'm telling you,
this punk punched me first!

620
00:49:01.465 --> 00:49:02.765
What?
Punk?

621
00:49:03.165 --> 00:49:04.219
Stop!

622
00:49:04.299 --> 00:49:05.385
What are you doing?

623
00:49:05.465 --> 00:49:07.165
Both of you!
Sit down!

624
00:49:09.032 --> 00:49:10.865
Give me your identification.

625
00:49:17.232 --> 00:49:20.619
Young man,
Let's wrap up quietly.

626
00:49:20.699 --> 00:49:22.010
Call your parents,

627
00:49:22.090 --> 00:49:24.285
it's not a big deal.

628
00:49:24.365 --> 00:49:25.832
Call them.

629
00:49:29.032 --> 00:49:31.119
What's this?

630
00:49:31.199 --> 00:49:34.299
You don't have parents?

631
00:49:37.732 --> 00:49:40.852
I knew it.
You orphan punk.

632
00:49:40.932 --> 00:49:43.119
He must have records.

633
00:49:43.199 --> 00:49:46.185
- You son of wench!
- Stop! Both of you!

634
00:49:46.265 --> 00:49:48.885
Sit down!

635
00:49:48.965 --> 00:49:50.485
Sit!

636
00:49:50.565 --> 00:49:51.785
Mister.

637
00:49:51.865 --> 00:49:53.411
One more word,

638
00:49:53.491 --> 00:49:55.919
I'll put you in jail.

639
00:49:55.999 --> 00:49:57.619
Excuse me, sir?

640
00:49:57.699 --> 00:49:59.519
Yes?

641
00:49:59.599 --> 00:50:02.185
I...

642
00:50:02.265 --> 00:50:04.699
I live with him, Han Ji Woong.

643
00:50:15.832 --> 00:50:17.952
Han Ji Woong.

644
00:50:18.032 --> 00:50:19.265
Is that true?

645
00:50:20.732 --> 00:50:21.899
I live with her.

646
00:50:23.265 --> 00:50:24.765
Punk.

647
00:50:25.632 --> 00:50:30.685
No matter
how shameful her job is!

648
00:50:30.765 --> 00:50:33.185
"I live with her"?
To your grandmother!

649
00:50:33.265 --> 00:50:34.785
What?

650
00:50:34.865 --> 00:50:36.585
Looks like your grandmother
took you

651
00:50:36.665 --> 00:50:38.385
after parents passed away!

652
00:50:38.465 --> 00:50:40.819
- It's not like that…
- Shut up.

653
00:50:40.899 --> 00:50:42.519
Mister.

654
00:50:42.599 --> 00:50:46.299
You pushed her first
in front of her grandson.

655
00:50:48.132 --> 00:50:52.685
You are so famous already.

656
00:50:52.765 --> 00:50:55.052
Look.

657
00:50:55.132 --> 00:50:57.752
You pushed old lady down
in mud, swearing.

658
00:50:57.832 --> 00:50:59.599
You were on the camera.

659
00:51:00.399 --> 00:51:01.599
Oh my!

660
00:51:02.099 --> 00:51:03.279
Who holds in it

661
00:51:03.359 --> 00:51:06.085
when this happens
to their grandmother?

662
00:51:06.165 --> 00:51:07.465
Seriously.

663
00:51:19.299 --> 00:51:21.799
Young man, Let's eat together.

664
00:51:27.999 --> 00:51:29.065
Have a seat.

665
00:51:48.299 --> 00:51:49.732
I'm sorry about the last night.

666
00:51:53.099 --> 00:51:55.365
I said awful things to you.

667
00:51:57.499 --> 00:51:58.799
I'm sorry.

668
00:52:01.099 --> 00:52:02.199
Let's eat.

669
00:52:12.399 --> 00:52:13.432
Are you alone?

670
00:52:17.732 --> 00:52:18.799
Yes.

671
00:52:21.132 --> 00:52:22.365
How?

672
00:52:24.799 --> 00:52:26.799
I've never met my parents.

673
00:52:31.965 --> 00:52:35.532
All right, let's eat.

674
00:53:11.932 --> 00:53:13.052
Where's Dae Hun?

675
00:53:13.132 --> 00:53:15.285
- Dea Hun?
- Yes.

676
00:53:15.365 --> 00:53:17.099
What are you talking about?

677
00:53:23.632 --> 00:53:25.319
Did you give him money?

678
00:53:25.399 --> 00:53:28.252
- Yes.
- Scumbag.

679
00:53:28.332 --> 00:53:30.232
Why didn't you call me?

680
00:53:30.865 --> 00:53:32.899
I trusted him.
And I was in trouble.

681
00:53:33.865 --> 00:53:35.285
What trouble?

682
00:53:35.365 --> 00:53:36.865
Never mind, it's okay now.

683
00:53:37.799 --> 00:53:39.419
Call me if you were in trouble.

684
00:53:39.499 --> 00:53:41.752
Don't bear it alone.

685
00:53:41.832 --> 00:53:43.065
Okay?

686
00:53:43.765 --> 00:53:44.965
Okay.

687
00:53:56.432 --> 00:54:00.052
I've put some more
for regulars, enjoy!

688
00:54:00.132 --> 00:54:01.652
Thank you.

689
00:54:01.732 --> 00:54:03.365
(Roast pork restaurant)

690
00:54:04.932 --> 00:54:06.668
We come here after every works,

691
00:54:06.748 --> 00:54:07.748
now we're regulars.

692
00:54:07.799 --> 00:54:10.152
Why?
Are you sick of it?

693
00:54:10.232 --> 00:54:13.410
This was our dream

694
00:54:13.490 --> 00:54:15.952
since we were in the orphanage.

695
00:54:16.032 --> 00:54:19.432
Eating with family was
the most envious thing.

696
00:54:22.432 --> 00:54:24.532
Today's house seemed
to be a young guy's.

697
00:54:26.265 --> 00:54:28.052
Right.

698
00:54:28.132 --> 00:54:30.065
He was 28-year-old.

699
00:54:31.199 --> 00:54:34.752
I guess the end of a lonely life

700
00:54:34.832 --> 00:54:37.732
has nothing to do with age.

701
00:54:39.532 --> 00:54:41.852
By the way, what's up with you?

702
00:54:41.932 --> 00:54:43.799
You've never bowed before.

703
00:54:45.432 --> 00:54:49.552
I looked into his stuff
and room,

704
00:54:49.632 --> 00:54:52.519
there was not much difference
between my room.

705
00:54:52.599 --> 00:54:54.031
They didn't think

706
00:54:54.890 --> 00:54:58.299
their last would be like that.

707
00:54:59.332 --> 00:55:03.365
While doing this job,
it makes me think a lot.

708
00:55:04.765 --> 00:55:07.399
People who leave this world alone,
at the last moment of them.

709
00:55:09.465 --> 00:55:14.332
If someone was there for them.

710
00:55:17.732 --> 00:55:19.852
Then,

711
00:55:19.932 --> 00:55:23.252
wouldn't they die feeling

712
00:55:23.332 --> 00:55:28.565
a little less fearful
and painful?

713
00:55:41.665 --> 00:55:44.685
How's the pet sitting?

714
00:55:44.765 --> 00:55:46.569
You almost lived with Happy

715
00:55:46.649 --> 00:55:48.952
at an orphanage,

716
00:55:49.032 --> 00:55:51.785
and you ended up with dogs.

717
00:55:51.865 --> 00:55:53.385
I love dogs.

718
00:55:53.465 --> 00:55:54.900
We can understand each other

719
00:55:54.980 --> 00:55:56.065
without talking.

720
00:56:01.799 --> 00:56:03.499
What are you doing?

721
00:56:04.365 --> 00:56:05.752
I'm disappointed.

722
00:56:05.832 --> 00:56:09.019
I'm lower than dogs to you.

723
00:56:09.099 --> 00:56:10.129
Without talking,

724
00:56:10.209 --> 00:56:11.499
you can't read my mind?

725
00:56:12.532 --> 00:56:15.485
Don't be like that.

726
00:56:15.565 --> 00:56:17.099
Stop it.

727
00:56:24.432 --> 00:56:25.999
It's good.

728
00:56:37.632 --> 00:56:41.265
(Nutritional supplements
Take one for breakfast and dinner)

729
00:57:08.699 --> 00:57:09.699
Hello, ma'am.

730
00:57:11.299 --> 00:57:12.519
Hello, ma'am.

731
00:57:12.599 --> 00:57:16.319
Where did you two go
so friendly?

732
00:57:16.399 --> 00:57:19.452
- Just walking.
- Walking?

733
00:57:19.532 --> 00:57:22.885
Unbelievable.

734
00:57:22.965 --> 00:57:25.619
Stop talking nonsense and go in.

735
00:57:25.699 --> 00:57:31.785
We're going on a picnic
at the park tomorrow.

736
00:57:31.865 --> 00:57:33.452
Do you want to go with us?

737
00:57:33.532 --> 00:57:34.619
A picnic?

738
00:57:34.699 --> 00:57:38.485
Yes, before Hyung Seok
joins the military.

739
00:57:38.565 --> 00:57:40.119
I'll visit on a break.

740
00:57:40.199 --> 00:57:41.765
You'd better!

741
00:57:43.265 --> 00:57:45.365
It's not far and really nice.

742
00:57:47.065 --> 00:57:48.452
Shall we?

743
00:57:48.532 --> 00:57:50.385
I have things to do.

744
00:57:50.465 --> 00:57:53.265
I'll help you,
let's go after that.

745
00:57:54.299 --> 00:57:56.452
Then, shall we?

746
00:57:56.532 --> 00:58:00.152
Yes, good.
Let's go.

747
00:58:00.232 --> 00:58:02.685
- Okay.
- Let's go to the mart.

748
00:58:02.765 --> 00:58:05.265
See you guys tomorrow.

749
00:58:19.965 --> 00:58:21.024
Should I cook eggs?

750
00:58:21.104 --> 00:58:22.719
Just sit down.

751
00:58:22.799 --> 00:58:25.299
- I can do the spinach!
- No, I got it.

752
00:58:26.632 --> 00:58:28.065
Well, you can try.

753
00:58:49.099 --> 00:58:51.885
Try not to burst.
That's good.

754
00:58:51.965 --> 00:58:54.432
You're good, Ji Woong.

755
00:58:56.099 --> 00:58:57.365
- Now this?
- Yes.

756
00:58:58.665 --> 00:59:00.932
Ta-da!

757
00:59:11.432 --> 00:59:12.932
Finished.

758
00:59:16.932 --> 00:59:18.665
It's so good, ma'am!

759
00:59:37.765 --> 00:59:39.785
Did you bring any delicious?

760
00:59:39.865 --> 00:59:40.952
No.

761
00:59:41.032 --> 00:59:42.352
Gimbap, fruits, cider.

762
00:59:42.432 --> 00:59:43.819
We have sandwiches!

763
00:59:43.899 --> 00:59:47.252
This old lady is so excited!

764
00:59:47.332 --> 00:59:49.219
Look at you, you're in trouble.

765
00:59:49.299 --> 00:59:51.719
- What trouble?
- I told you.

766
00:59:51.799 --> 00:59:53.301
If a person changes,

767
00:59:53.381 --> 00:59:54.619
it's time to go.

768
00:59:54.699 --> 00:59:56.373
Go where?

769
00:59:56.453 --> 00:59:58.852
I can't afford to go anywhere.

770
00:59:58.932 --> 01:00:01.419
The Grim Reaper won't take you

771
01:00:01.499 --> 01:00:04.899
because you don't spend a money.

772
01:00:09.799 --> 01:00:11.599
We'll be right back.

773
01:00:11.732 --> 01:00:13.152
Where are you going?

774
01:00:13.232 --> 01:00:14.232
Buy something.

775
01:00:19.432 --> 01:00:23.232
They look happy to be on picnic.

776
01:00:24.565 --> 01:00:26.419
He's good, right?

777
01:00:26.499 --> 01:00:28.619
Yes, he's pure.

778
01:00:28.699 --> 01:00:31.452
He has a little dark
because he had been alone,

779
01:00:31.532 --> 01:00:33.819
but he's one pure kid.

780
01:00:33.899 --> 01:00:36.652
But Ji Hun came in…

781
01:00:36.732 --> 01:00:40.519
Ji Woong!
Not Ji Hun.

782
01:00:40.599 --> 01:00:43.685
Whatever, Ji Hun, Ji Woong.

783
01:00:43.765 --> 01:00:45.465
It's same to me.

784
01:00:47.799 --> 01:00:52.585
You've changed.

785
01:00:52.665 --> 01:00:56.132
Sitting out here at this time.

786
01:00:56.799 --> 01:00:58.585
Have I?

787
01:00:58.665 --> 01:01:04.732
Let's come out and look
around the world sometimes.

788
01:01:05.632 --> 01:01:07.065
That's not so bad.

789
01:01:12.532 --> 01:01:16.085
The park is big, right?

790
01:01:16.165 --> 01:01:17.665
The sunshine is nice.

791
01:01:18.465 --> 01:01:20.919
You're right.

792
01:01:20.999 --> 01:01:23.519
It's a road I passed every day,

793
01:01:23.599 --> 01:01:28.319
I felt it's irrelevant to me.

794
01:01:28.399 --> 01:01:30.099
But not today.

795
01:01:36.265 --> 01:01:38.632
I've heard about her
from my grandmother.

796
01:01:41.465 --> 01:01:44.019
She used to be
a really bright person.

797
01:01:44.099 --> 01:01:46.419
They went
to the same university.

798
01:01:46.499 --> 01:01:49.285
My grandmother got married
after she graduated,

799
01:01:49.365 --> 01:01:51.132
and Gum Bun went to Germany.

800
01:01:52.799 --> 01:01:54.039
They understand each other well

801
01:01:54.101 --> 01:01:55.285
without talking,

802
01:01:55.365 --> 01:01:56.685
I think that's
why they are close.

803
01:01:58.499 --> 01:01:59.875
Let's go,
they must be waiting for us.

804
01:01:59.899 --> 01:02:01.032
Yes.

805
01:02:03.232 --> 01:02:04.257
Here.

806
01:02:04.337 --> 01:02:06.032
They made it together.

807
01:02:10.799 --> 01:02:11.719
Try this.

808
01:02:11.799 --> 01:02:14.685
This is why I fake
diseases sometimes.

809
01:02:14.765 --> 01:02:16.365
Let's take a picture.

810
01:02:17.199 --> 01:02:18.375
Grandmother,
shall we make a heart?

811
01:02:18.399 --> 01:02:19.932
A heart?
Yes!

812
01:02:22.199 --> 01:02:24.219
Ready?
Focus on here.

813
01:02:24.299 --> 01:02:29.365
More friendly, smile, 1,2,3!

814
01:02:36.799 --> 01:02:38.199
Do you want
to see pictures of Jing?

815
01:02:43.132 --> 01:02:44.819
Look.

816
01:02:44.899 --> 01:02:46.032
So cute.

817
01:02:47.199 --> 01:02:49.799
- I miss him.
- So cute, isn't he?

818
01:02:50.465 --> 01:02:53.885
“It's better to have loved
and lost,

819
01:02:53.965 --> 01:02:57.619
than never to have loved
at all.”

820
01:02:57.699 --> 01:02:58.752
Excuse me?

821
01:02:58.832 --> 01:03:01.452
It's better to lose everything

822
01:03:01.532 --> 01:03:05.119
by making love
than not loving it.

823
01:03:05.199 --> 01:03:06.309
Understand?

824
01:03:06.389 --> 01:03:09.899
No, we're just friends.

825
01:03:10.432 --> 01:03:12.419
You're too soft.

826
01:03:12.499 --> 01:03:14.152
It's a habit to lose.

827
01:03:14.232 --> 01:03:15.685
You must win when you can.

828
01:03:15.765 --> 01:03:18.265
- Coffee bet, 1 point!
- Cheeky.

829
01:03:19.399 --> 01:03:21.365
- Hello, professor.
- Professor?

830
01:03:24.165 --> 01:03:28.052
I won!
I finally won!

831
01:03:28.132 --> 01:03:29.885
You can't put up
with it too much.

832
01:03:29.965 --> 01:03:31.452
You have to say
what you must say.

833
01:03:31.532 --> 01:03:34.185
Ji Woong,
I'm going to drink some coffee.

834
01:03:34.265 --> 01:03:35.665
Please take care of this.

835
01:03:37.399 --> 01:03:39.285
I'd love to drink coffee.

836
01:03:39.365 --> 01:03:41.565
Don't let them
take advantage of you.

837
01:03:43.499 --> 01:03:46.199
Sorry.
I was too harsh on you.

838
01:03:47.565 --> 01:03:48.752
Have some fun!

839
01:03:48.832 --> 01:03:50.932
That's how you gain more energy!

840
01:03:56.632 --> 01:03:58.852
- It's so good.
- As expected, Han river is...

841
01:03:58.932 --> 01:04:01.519
So, what's your dream?

842
01:04:01.599 --> 01:04:04.032
I'd like to run
a pet sitting business properly.

843
01:04:07.032 --> 01:04:08.852
An apartment?

844
01:04:08.932 --> 01:04:10.299
Yes, at the living space.

845
01:04:24.432 --> 01:04:26.051
For the last time.

846
01:04:26.131 --> 01:04:27.163
Please borrow me $500!

847
01:04:27.243 --> 01:04:28.276
How dare you.

848
01:04:28.356 --> 01:04:30.719
It's an emergency.

849
01:04:30.799 --> 01:04:32.719
Bullcrap, pay back the money
you borrowed before.

850
01:04:32.799 --> 01:04:34.599
Ji Woong!

851
01:05:16.432 --> 01:05:17.619
What are these?

852
01:05:17.699 --> 01:05:18.825
I used to eat a long time ago,

853
01:05:18.849 --> 01:05:20.209
but I wonder
if it tastes the same.

854
01:05:20.565 --> 01:05:21.885
Pannfisch.

855
01:05:21.965 --> 01:05:23.899
Sauerkraut.

856
01:05:26.065 --> 01:05:27.785
It's delicious!

857
01:05:27.865 --> 01:05:29.284
I was poor,

858
01:05:29.364 --> 01:05:30.604
I made it because it was cheap.

859
01:05:31.132 --> 01:05:32.985
I liked the taste.

860
01:05:33.065 --> 01:05:34.819
I forgot about it,

861
01:05:34.899 --> 01:05:37.352
but it suddenly came to mind.

862
01:05:37.432 --> 01:05:40.032
Go ahead,
don't mind what old lady says.

863
01:05:49.565 --> 01:05:50.565
I enjoyed the food.

864
01:05:50.632 --> 01:05:52.619
Stop, you don't need to anymore.

865
01:05:52.699 --> 01:05:55.252
No!
I insist.

866
01:05:55.332 --> 01:05:59.652
So I can have more sometimes.

867
01:05:59.732 --> 01:06:03.599
Your food makes
my stomach comfortable.

868
01:06:29.899 --> 01:06:31.141
Were you looking
at the picture again?

869
01:06:31.165 --> 01:06:33.499
Yes.

870
01:06:35.399 --> 01:06:37.691
Since Hyung Seok left home,

871
01:06:37.771 --> 01:06:39.319
I feel so empty.

872
01:06:39.399 --> 01:06:41.040
I brought this、

873
01:06:41.120 --> 01:06:42.641
because I thought
you'd be acting pitiful.

874
01:06:42.665 --> 01:06:44.732
A porridge?

875
01:06:47.432 --> 01:06:49.885
Abalone porridge?

876
01:06:49.965 --> 01:06:51.732
It's not a bad idea
to fake illness.

877
01:06:52.565 --> 01:06:53.975
A serious illness begins
with the heart.

878
01:06:53.999 --> 01:06:57.052
Shake it off and go outside!

879
01:06:57.132 --> 01:07:00.419
Yes, nurse.

880
01:07:00.499 --> 01:07:01.752
Don't be absurd.

881
01:07:01.832 --> 01:07:03.419
I'm not.

882
01:07:03.499 --> 01:07:06.699
If it weren't for you,
I would never see my grandson.

883
01:07:07.632 --> 01:07:09.452
It's a long time ago.

884
01:07:09.532 --> 01:07:12.519
Acute myocardial infarction?

885
01:07:12.599 --> 01:07:15.485
Golden time is an hour.

886
01:07:15.565 --> 01:07:17.985
How do ordinary people
know that?

887
01:07:18.065 --> 01:07:20.399
You did
because you were a nurse.

888
01:07:22.232 --> 01:07:25.452
Time flies when you look back.

889
01:07:25.532 --> 01:07:28.319
It feels like yesterday
when we were a freshman.

890
01:07:28.399 --> 01:07:30.585
You mean it's time to leave.

891
01:07:30.665 --> 01:07:32.769
Okay!

892
01:07:32.849 --> 01:07:35.032
I'll stop, stay a little more!

893
01:07:38.799 --> 01:07:41.532
Sickness makes me
recall old times.

894
01:07:48.899 --> 01:07:51.652
The porridge
on the table is for you.

895
01:07:51.732 --> 01:07:53.632
No charge this time!

896
01:08:15.132 --> 01:08:16.365
What are you doing?

897
01:08:16.899 --> 01:08:18.999
I cleaned your room too.

898
01:08:42.499 --> 01:08:43.999
What's wrong?

899
01:08:55.299 --> 01:08:57.885
Why is this here?

900
01:08:57.965 --> 01:08:59.385
I don't know, what is it?

901
01:08:59.465 --> 01:09:02.932
Even with the evidence,
do you deny it?

902
01:09:04.399 --> 01:09:05.885
Get out.

903
01:09:05.965 --> 01:09:07.632
Get out of my house, right now!

904
01:09:37.199 --> 01:09:38.532
Let's go to your place.

905
01:10:17.765 --> 01:10:20.299
What?
What?

906
01:10:24.365 --> 01:10:26.219
Okay, I got it.

907
01:10:26.299 --> 01:10:27.219
Calm down, first.

908
01:10:27.299 --> 01:10:28.865
You pathetic son of wench!

909
01:10:30.265 --> 01:10:32.065
I said calm down.

910
01:10:34.099 --> 01:10:39.452
Ji Woong, calm down.
Listen to me.

911
01:10:39.532 --> 01:10:40.565
Bullcrap!

912
01:10:46.732 --> 01:10:48.865
Give me my money back!

913
01:10:50.532 --> 01:10:51.965
I can't.

914
01:10:52.632 --> 01:10:53.632
Scumbag.

915
01:10:53.665 --> 01:10:55.965
I'll be locked up in jail
without it.

916
01:10:58.299 --> 01:10:59.466
What?

917
01:11:00.548 --> 01:11:02.452
I needed money.

918
01:11:02.532 --> 01:11:04.765
So I committed fraud
on the used market.

919
01:11:07.032 --> 01:11:08.299
What?

920
01:11:15.599 --> 01:11:17.532
- Min Chul.
- Are you with him?

921
01:11:18.065 --> 01:11:20.752
- Yes.
- What did he do, this time?

922
01:11:20.832 --> 01:11:23.185
I think we should pay back
to the victims first.

923
01:11:23.265 --> 01:11:26.185
Yeah, I'll handle it,
don't worry.

924
01:11:26.265 --> 01:11:28.465
Okay.

925
01:11:48.432 --> 01:11:49.899
I'm sorry.

926
01:11:51.265 --> 01:11:53.465
I must have been crazy.

927
01:11:56.899 --> 01:11:59.319
I'm sorry, ma'am.

928
01:11:59.399 --> 01:12:00.765
Please forgive me.

929
01:12:02.565 --> 01:12:03.999
I'm sorry.

930
01:12:13.399 --> 01:12:19.365
Right after high school.
They said we're adults.

931
01:12:20.499 --> 01:12:25.152
They told us to leave
because we were 20 years old.

932
01:12:25.232 --> 01:12:26.332
To where?

933
01:12:30.365 --> 01:12:32.432
How?

934
01:12:35.065 --> 01:12:36.852
Do you…

935
01:12:36.932 --> 01:12:39.565
Remember $5,000 you get
when we went out?

936
01:12:42.465 --> 01:12:44.665
I thought it was freaking a lot.

937
01:12:48.332 --> 01:12:50.419
But while living
in a small room,

938
01:12:50.499 --> 01:12:51.999
It disappeared quickly.

939
01:12:54.032 --> 01:12:55.965
That's why you did it?

940
01:12:58.065 --> 01:12:59.519
“Because you're an orphan.”

941
01:12:59.599 --> 01:13:02.652
“Because you don't have
any parents.”

942
01:13:02.732 --> 01:13:04.599
Do you want to hear
something like that?

943
01:13:11.965 --> 01:13:15.119
When we were in school,

944
01:13:15.199 --> 01:13:17.124
remember they looked at us

945
01:13:17.204 --> 01:13:19.165
even if a tiny eraser disappeared?

946
01:13:21.399 --> 01:13:29.219
You're smartass,
goes to university.

947
01:13:29.299 --> 01:13:31.232
You know nothing.

948
01:13:33.132 --> 01:13:35.032
It was the easiest way.

949
01:13:37.099 --> 01:13:39.432
They love a model student.

950
01:13:43.032 --> 01:13:45.265
They love an obedient child!

951
01:13:52.599 --> 01:13:55.232
You freaking loved to be loved.

952
01:13:56.532 --> 01:13:59.452
Must've been feeling
so freaking good…

953
01:13:59.532 --> 01:14:02.899
University is the same.

954
01:14:03.999 --> 01:14:06.385
When my friends…

955
01:14:06.465 --> 01:14:14.465
ask me about my parents,

956
01:14:14.999 --> 01:14:16.999
I have nothing to say.

957
01:14:19.065 --> 01:14:22.652
Say about their moms,

958
01:14:22.732 --> 01:14:25.132
what does your dad do...

959
01:14:27.065 --> 01:14:29.732
I thought it would be different
in university.

960
01:14:30.399 --> 01:14:32.699
But It's all the same.

961
01:14:34.299 --> 01:14:39.099
It's branded on us forever.

962
01:14:42.432 --> 01:14:43.865
An orphan.

963
01:14:57.665 --> 01:15:00.019
Hey.
What's wrong with you?

964
01:15:00.099 --> 01:15:02.852
- Ji Woong, Come on.
- Hey, guys.

965
01:15:02.932 --> 01:15:06.132
- Let's go.
- No, let me go.

966
01:15:08.265 --> 01:15:10.299
It's a school!

967
01:15:12.265 --> 01:15:14.085
- Hey!
- Let go of me.

968
01:15:14.165 --> 01:15:17.865
- You wacko!
- I got to run.

969
01:15:24.432 --> 01:15:25.465
Listen guys.

970
01:15:26.599 --> 01:15:28.452
Let me tell you a funny story.

971
01:15:28.532 --> 01:15:30.165
Yes, go ahead.

972
01:15:30.765 --> 01:15:33.575
Do you know what I did on the day

973
01:15:33.655 --> 01:15:34.935
I took Scholastic Aptitude Test?

974
01:15:37.265 --> 01:15:39.352
After the exam,

975
01:15:39.432 --> 01:15:41.432
I went to my part-time job.

976
01:15:42.765 --> 01:15:46.619
Others were happy
because exams are over.

977
01:15:46.699 --> 01:15:49.852
But I couldn't.

978
01:15:49.932 --> 01:15:52.665
We couldn't celebrate.

979
01:15:54.599 --> 01:15:56.965
We had to leave the orphanage.

980
01:16:00.565 --> 01:16:02.232
I don't have mom and dad!

981
01:16:03.332 --> 01:16:04.499
I'm alone!

982
01:16:07.699 --> 01:16:10.852
Generation pause?

983
01:16:10.932 --> 01:16:16.785
I'm not paused.
I'm N.

984
01:16:16.865 --> 01:16:18.832
Because I have nothing.

985
01:16:33.865 --> 01:16:35.452
This is why he's an idiot.

986
01:16:35.532 --> 01:16:37.785
Why would you hide that
for 2 years, you idiot.

987
01:16:37.865 --> 01:16:39.685
Yes, What's wrong with that?

988
01:16:39.765 --> 01:16:43.732
Ji Woong, it's not your fault
that you grew up in an orphanage.

989
01:16:45.799 --> 01:16:48.719
Sung Jin, let's kidnap him
during this summer vacation.

990
01:16:48.799 --> 01:16:50.485
- Call?
- Call.

991
01:16:50.565 --> 01:16:52.619
Let's kidnap him
and torture him.

992
01:16:52.699 --> 01:16:54.419
Don't let him work.

993
01:16:54.499 --> 01:16:56.785
You know he's going crazy
if he can't work, right?

994
01:16:56.865 --> 01:17:00.099
I know, a workaholic is worse
than an alcoholic.

995
01:17:06.399 --> 01:17:07.899
Hello?

996
01:17:16.332 --> 01:17:22.032
(Rest in peace)

997
01:18:58.799 --> 01:19:00.265
You'll be okay?

998
01:19:08.632 --> 01:19:09.865
See you later.

999
01:19:41.232 --> 01:19:42.652
What are you looking for?

1000
01:19:42.732 --> 01:19:44.832
It's nothing.

1001
01:19:46.632 --> 01:19:48.585
She should've given us
in advance.

1002
01:19:48.665 --> 01:19:50.099
What if there's none?

1003
01:19:50.832 --> 01:19:54.599
Come on.

1004
01:19:57.565 --> 01:19:59.294
What if the student

1005
01:19:59.374 --> 01:20:00.865
who lived with my mom took it?

1006
01:20:02.265 --> 01:20:03.485
Excuse me, sir.

1007
01:20:03.565 --> 01:20:05.385
Most of them will burn.

1008
01:20:05.465 --> 01:20:07.035
Please take things

1009
01:20:07.115 --> 01:20:08.275
for remembering the deceased.

1010
01:20:08.399 --> 01:20:09.399
Yes.

1011
01:20:13.199 --> 01:20:16.285
Do you want to burn
these pictures and frames?

1012
01:20:16.365 --> 01:20:17.532
Yes, do it.

1013
01:20:18.732 --> 01:20:20.685
Please take this frame.

1014
01:20:20.765 --> 01:20:23.865
These are the pictures
that your mother valued the most.

1015
01:20:24.799 --> 01:20:26.452
Sir?
How about this?

1016
01:20:26.532 --> 01:20:27.532
Yes?

1017
01:20:31.199 --> 01:20:32.299
Looking for this?

1018
01:20:33.599 --> 01:20:34.599
Yes?

1019
01:20:39.799 --> 01:20:43.519
It's nothing.

1020
01:20:43.599 --> 01:20:47.752
It was right in front of us.

1021
01:20:47.832 --> 01:20:51.852
She thought
at least you would take it.

1022
01:20:51.932 --> 01:20:54.999
She always missed the moment
spent with you.

1023
01:22:00.999 --> 01:22:04.565
I finally graduated
from college,

1024
01:22:06.465 --> 01:22:08.399
but my family was
having a hard time.

1025
01:22:11.699 --> 01:22:13.365
I went to Germany as a nurse.

1026
01:22:20.199 --> 01:22:22.540
They gave me eight times

1027
01:22:23.532 --> 01:22:25.032
more of normal salary.

1028
01:22:26.765 --> 01:22:30.552
Leaving my country,

1029
01:22:30.632 --> 01:22:33.299
I worked in deathly agony.

1030
01:22:38.665 --> 01:22:43.765
From there,
I met someone I loved.

1031
01:22:48.199 --> 01:22:51.165
But turns out,
he was a married man.

1032
01:22:55.199 --> 01:22:57.265
Eventually, he abandoned me.

1033
01:22:58.799 --> 01:23:02.065
I came back to my mother.

1034
01:23:02.999 --> 01:23:05.095
My father spent my money

1035
01:23:05.394 --> 01:23:07.832
drinking and cheating on mom.

1036
01:23:09.165 --> 01:23:14.852
My mom died because of my father

1037
01:23:14.932 --> 01:23:17.432
in exasperation and depression.

1038
01:23:21.299 --> 01:23:23.232
I felt disillusioned.

1039
01:23:24.765 --> 01:23:26.699
There was no one I can trust.

1040
01:23:28.132 --> 01:23:31.465
I thought about killing myself,

1041
01:23:34.332 --> 01:23:37.052
but I wasn't…

1042
01:23:37.132 --> 01:23:39.099
brutal enough.

1043
01:23:44.465 --> 01:23:47.299
That's why I'm still living.

1044
01:23:48.799 --> 01:23:50.132
Alone.

1045
01:23:59.999 --> 01:24:02.685
I've never waited

1046
01:24:02.765 --> 01:24:04.665
for anyone.

1047
01:24:11.499 --> 01:24:13.485
He's late.

1048
01:24:13.565 --> 01:24:15.932
He should call if he's late.

1049
01:24:21.599 --> 01:24:22.765
Young man?

1050
01:24:26.399 --> 01:24:28.419
Concerned…

1051
01:24:28.499 --> 01:24:30.065
Missing…

1052
01:24:38.532 --> 01:24:42.285
A month after I was born

1053
01:24:42.365 --> 01:24:44.599
I was abandoned at church.

1054
01:24:47.532 --> 01:24:50.932
Without knowing
the name or birthday,

1055
01:24:51.599 --> 01:24:53.965
I was sent to an orphanage.

1056
01:24:55.899 --> 01:24:58.552
My birthday is the day

1057
01:24:58.632 --> 01:25:00.599
I was abandoned at church.

1058
01:25:04.765 --> 01:25:06.199
My family name is Han.

1059
01:25:09.299 --> 01:25:11.965
Because the principal's
last name is Han.

1060
01:25:16.999 --> 01:25:21.185
The thing I hate the most is

1061
01:25:21.265 --> 01:25:25.185
writing mom and dad's names

1062
01:25:25.265 --> 01:25:26.765
and jobs.

1063
01:25:29.865 --> 01:25:31.399
It's so hard.

1064
01:25:34.665 --> 01:25:36.899
To someone like me.

1065
01:25:40.965 --> 01:25:42.065
Ji Woong.

1066
01:25:47.332 --> 01:25:51.665
Do you want to live with me?

1067
01:25:57.165 --> 01:25:59.099
As a family.

1068
01:26:01.265 --> 01:26:03.099
A real family.

1069
01:26:07.932 --> 01:26:10.885
It may not be enough for you

1070
01:26:10.965 --> 01:26:12.832
but as your grandmother.

1071
01:26:15.599 --> 01:26:17.619
To me,

1072
01:26:17.699 --> 01:26:21.019
you are a university student,
handsome,

1073
01:26:21.099 --> 01:26:22.765
and my undeserved grandson.

1074
01:26:25.565 --> 01:26:26.885
Why?

1075
01:26:26.965 --> 01:26:28.599
Concerned…

1076
01:26:35.132 --> 01:26:36.852
I may not look like it,

1077
01:26:36.932 --> 01:26:39.292
but I graduated University
of Foreign Studies, major German.

1078
01:26:56.665 --> 01:27:01.785
(The first family
of Room Sharing Program)

1079
01:27:01.865 --> 01:27:04.485
Hi, nice to see you.

1080
01:27:04.565 --> 01:27:05.565
Concerned…

1081
01:27:07.732 --> 01:27:09.285
During the Room Sharing Program,

1082
01:27:09.365 --> 01:27:12.685
A beautiful thing happened
that fits the purpose of us.

1083
01:27:12.765 --> 01:27:18.399
We are here to hold a small event
to celebrate this occasion.

1084
01:27:19.765 --> 01:27:21.699
Are you ready?

1085
01:27:26.065 --> 01:27:28.632
(Affidavit family relationship)

1086
01:27:30.065 --> 01:27:32.219
Now, everybody together,

1087
01:27:32.299 --> 01:27:34.619
count 1,2,3.

1088
01:27:34.699 --> 01:27:36.085
Let's get started right away!

1089
01:27:36.165 --> 01:27:38.352
Shout it out loud!

1090
01:27:38.432 --> 01:27:41.402
One! Two! Three!

1091
01:27:41.482 --> 01:27:43.232
Congratulations!

1092
01:27:44.932 --> 01:27:46.632
Give them a round of applause!

1093
01:27:49.899 --> 01:27:51.399
Please give them a big hand.

1094
01:28:02.632 --> 01:28:04.499
Congratulations!

1095
01:28:20.132 --> 01:28:22.219
Ji Woong!
Wake up.

1096
01:28:22.299 --> 01:28:24.652
I'm tired, grandmother.

1097
01:28:24.732 --> 01:28:26.452
A few minutes more.

1098
01:28:26.532 --> 01:28:28.372
You said you'd get fired
if you were late again

1099
01:28:42.899 --> 01:28:45.285
Why are you saying it so hard?

1100
01:28:45.365 --> 01:28:46.465
I thought you already knew.

1101
01:28:48.965 --> 01:28:50.699
Enjoy your meal.

1102
01:29:16.765 --> 01:29:18.488
Don't be picky.

1103
01:29:18.568 --> 01:29:19.585
I'll come again tomorrow.

1104
01:29:19.665 --> 01:29:21.799
- Okay.
- Good kids.

1105
01:29:28.232 --> 01:29:31.219
I can't move
because I'm not feeling well.

1106
01:29:31.299 --> 01:29:33.452
With this medicine,
I can put up with it.

1107
01:29:33.532 --> 01:29:35.332
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

1108
01:29:35.765 --> 01:29:36.899
Thank you.

1109
01:29:47.799 --> 01:29:48.885
Grandmother!

1110
01:29:48.965 --> 01:29:50.852
Why don't you stop
picking up boxes?

1111
01:29:50.932 --> 01:29:52.752
I'm afraid
there'll be another accident!

1112
01:29:52.832 --> 01:29:54.752
If you don't move,
you'll get older faster!

1113
01:29:54.832 --> 01:29:57.399
I have to gather a small things
to help the children!

1114
01:30:11.665 --> 01:30:13.052
Hello, ma'am.

1115
01:30:13.132 --> 01:30:14.319
Deposit please.

1116
01:30:14.399 --> 01:30:15.408
(Save the children
A meal for the kids)

1117
01:30:15.432 --> 01:30:17.999
Here is the new bank account
for self-reliance support funds.

1118
01:30:23.265 --> 01:30:26.632
(Han Ji Woong)

1119
01:30:30.832 --> 01:30:32.799
(Defecation not allowed)

1120
01:30:41.432 --> 01:30:43.565
(My Perfect Roommate)
